# Native Bamboo for Fcitx 5

A Vietnamese input method addon with a native C++ engine. Building and running
this version requires no Go compiler, cgo bridge, or Go runtime.

See [INSTALL.md](INSTALL.md) for Ubuntu 26.04 dependencies, build, installation,
desktop activation, troubleshooting, and removal instructions.

The native port preserves Bamboo's built-in input methods, custom keymaps,
spelling and dictionary checks, macros, restoration, tone options, and output
charsets. Existing Fcitx Bamboo configuration files continue to work.

## Architecture

- `bamboo/native/`: independently buildable C++17 processing library and adapter;
  ICU provides Unicode classification and simple case conversion.
- `src/`: Fcitx addon using typed C++ objects and immutable dictionary/macro
  snapshots. The Fcitx build uses the C++ standard required by its development
  package (C++20 on Ubuntu 26.04).
- `data/`, `po/`: dictionary, icon, and translations.
- `tests/`: isolated Fcitx test-frontend integration test.
- Legacy Go sources and the old core submodule are reference material only.
  Neither submodule initialization nor a sibling core checkout is needed to build.

## Tests

Run `ctest --test-dir build-native --output-on-failure` after the full build.
The checked-in fixtures replay the original Go core tests and deterministic
corpora across every built-in input method. Additional fixtures compare adapter
acceptance, preedit, commits, configuration options, custom rules, utilities,
and every output charset. Tests also exercise independent contexts, reload
ownership, dictionary reading, and malformed custom definitions.

Core-only development needs CMake, a C++17 compiler, and ICU development headers:

```sh
cmake -S bamboo/native -B build-core -DCMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=Release
cmake --build build-core
ctest --test-dir build-core --output-on-failure
```

For sanitizer checks, add these flags when configuring a fresh build directory:

```sh
-DCMAKE_CXX_FLAGS="-fsanitize=address,undefined -fno-omit-frame-pointer" \
-DCMAKE_EXE_LINKER_FLAGS="-fsanitize=address,undefined"
```

Go and Python are needed only to regenerate reference material. With the original
`bamboo-core` checkout available, run:

```sh
python3 tools/import-go-tables.py ../bamboo-core
python3 tools/generate-fixtures.py ../bamboo-core
clang-format -i bamboo/native/data.cpp
```

The fixture generator runs the original Go tests before exporting their behavior.
Do not regenerate fixtures to conceal an unexplained native mismatch. Format C++
changes with the repository's `.clang-format`.

